WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/components/forms/CurrencyInput.tsx (216 lines) + its core web/src/lib/currencyFormat.ts (316 lines).
  A fully CONTROLLED, currency-aware text field:
    • Canonical storage = integer micro-units (1 major unit = 1_000_000) to avoid FP round-trip loss across
      currencies with 0/2/3/4 fractional digits (USD/JPY/BHD/CLF).
    • Renders `Intl.NumberFormat` currency display (symbol, fixed digits, grouping OFF for the field) + a decorative
      (aria-hidden) currency-symbol icon; `aria-label` (required `ariaLabel` prop) labels the input.
    • Parses user text on blur / Enter, accepting: the localized symbol on EITHER side ("$1.50", "1,50 €"), the
      literal ISO code ("USD 1.50"), locale group separators ("1,234.56" en-US, "1.234,56" de-DE), and accounting
      parentheses for negatives ("($1.50)" → -1.5); renormalises the visible text to the canonical-rounded form.
    • Re-syncs the local text buffer from the parent's `valueMicro` ONLY when the field is not focused, so an
      external change never clobbers in-progress typing (the `focusedRef` guard).
  Helpers (reproduced verbatim — arithmetic is the contract):
    valueToMicro(v)   = (v==null||!finite) ? null : Math.round(v*1e6)   (round half toward +∞);
    microToValue(m)   = (m==null) ? null : m/1e6;
    formatCurrencyValue(v) = (v==null||!finite) ? "" : Intl currency (digits=clampPrecision, grouping off);
                        invalid ISO code (RangeError) ⇒ "{CODE} {plain decimal}";
    currencySymbol    = the localized symbol; invalid code ⇒ the code verbatim;
    parseCurrencyText = trim → accounting parens → strip symbol + ISO code (case-insensitive) → collapse leading
                        sign → parseLocaleNumber; blank/non-finite ⇒ null;
    parseLocaleNumber = strip the locale group separator (incl. NBSP/space), decimal separator → '.';
    currencyCodeFromSymbol = 21-entry symbol→ISO map, default USD; clampPrecision = null⇒2 else clamp 0..20.
  Hooks  : (none — pure presentational component; the prompt's "Data sources: none"). The value flows through the
           parent via props, not a TanStack query.
  i18n   : the web component takes its accessibility label from the caller (`ariaLabel`); its documented example is
           the settings "Electricity Cost (per kWh)" field. Per the native no-English-literals rule that example is
           promoted to a P1/S10 key (table "CurrencyInput") and used as the default label.

