PARITY MAPPING  (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported, no raw hex)
  <Input value icon aria-label>     → CurrencyFieldView: HStack { CurrencySymbolGlyph ; TextField } + token chrome
  symbol span (aria-hidden)         → CurrencySymbolGlyph .accessibilityHidden(true), Font.TS.bodySm / textMuted
  Intl currency (grouping off)      → CurrencyFormat.formatCurrencyValue (NumberFormatter .currency, usesGrouping
                                      false, min=max fraction digits = clampPrecision)
  invalid code fallback             → "{code} {decimalString}" (web "{CODE} {plain}")
  Math.round(v*1e6)                 → valueToMicro floor(v*1e6 + 0.5) (half toward +∞, exact JS parity)
  parse symbol/ISO/parens/sign      → parseCurrencyText (strip both sides, case-insensitive code, ($..) negative,
                                      leading -/+ collapse) — each unit-asserted
  locale group/decimal separators   → parseLocaleNumber (NumberFormatter groupingSeparator/decimalSeparator,
                                      NBSP/narrow-NBSP/space collapse)
  focusedRef no-clobber resync      → CurrencyInputModel.applyExternal (value always; text only when !isEditing)
  commit on blur/Enter              → endEditing (blur) + onSubmit→commit (Enter), both renormalise the buffer
  ariaLabel / disabled props        → model.accessibilityLabel (i18n) / model.isEnabled (.disabled + dim)
  i18n                              → every string via CurrencyInputStrings (NSLocalizedString table, web literal
                                      as value: fallback); rendered Text(verbatim:)
  a11y                              → field carries .accessibilityLabel + .accessibilityValue (entered text or the
                                      empty announcement); symbol hidden; Dynamic Type via Font.TS; Reduce Motion
                                      via TSFadeIn; iOS decimal keypad
  telemetry                         → view.opened surface="CurrencyInput" emitted once on first appear (P1/S11)

STATES (every state present in the web source renders — no hidden surface)
  empty    → no canonical value → the symbol glyph + the localized prompt (web blank <Input>); never a blank box.
  value    → a formatted / in-progress amount (USD/EUR/JPY/BHD covered in previews + tests).
  editing  → focus-preserving: an external value change while typing updates the canonical value but does NOT
             clobber the buffer (testExternalChangeDoesNotClobberInProgressText).
  disabled → web `disabled` passthrough → a dimmed, non-editable field.
  invalid-currency fallback → a non-ISO-4217 code renders "{CODE} {decimal}" (testInvalidCurrency...).
  N/A (documented, not skipped): loading / error / stale / offline. The web source is a PURE controlled input with
  NO data source (prompt "Data sources: none — pure presentational component"; "Charts/maps: none"); there is no
  async fetch to load, fail, go stale, or lose connectivity. These template states have no web-source branch to
  reproduce, so reproducing them would be inventing UI the spec does not have. The one applicable template state,
  `empty`, IS implemented as a first-class branch (CurrencyFieldPhase.empty + the empty VoiceOver announcement).

